engine_change: `kernel/DiSyL/v4/Parser.php` no longer skips an entire balanced `{...}` block when it fails `looksLikeDisyl()` inside raw-text elements. It emits/scans the opening brace as plain text one character at a time, allowing nested DiSyL expressions to be discovered. The existing discriminator remains unchanged, preserving CSS declarations and `${...}` template literals as raw text. Include-stack handling was untouched.

